                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>The School of Interdisciplinary and Trans-Disciplinary Studies (SOITS) was   established to develop academic programmes and courses that address the complex dynamics of multi-faceted social issues and processes. The School functions as an enabling space to foster interdisciplinary academic studies and research drawing upon theoretical, empirical and methodological resources cutting across disciplinary boundaries. The School promotes interactive academic co-existence amongst scholars of diverse specializations facilitating convergence of disciplines and transactional mutuality of holistic wisdom. The programmes offered by the School are in the area of Environmental Studies, Philosophy,Folklore and Culture, Sustainability Science, Diaspora Studies. The School offers Ph.D. programmes in Interdisciplinary and Trans-disciplinary Studies and Environmental Sciences along with 7 Masters Programmes, 6 Post Graduate Diploma, 1 Bachelors, 2 Certificate and 1 Awareness Programme. The School also offers 4 online programmes and 11 MOOCs (Massive Open Online Course). </p>
<p><b>Vision: </b>“To develop the school as an enabling space to foster interdisciplinary academic studies and research drawing upon theoretical, empirical and methodological resources cutting across disciplinary boundaries. To promote interactive academic co-existence amongst scholars of diverse specializations facilitating convergence of disciplines and transactional mutuality of holistic wisdom.”</p>
<p><b>Mission: </b>“To develop academic programmes and courses that addresses the complex dynamics of multi-faceted social issues and processes. To strengthen the social extension aspect of research and facilitate issue based production of knowledge through incessant interaction with and participation of people.”</p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Objectives"  ><p><ul>
<li>To develop academic programmes and courses that provide holistic and all round personality development of the learners.</li>
<li>To encourage dialogue and discussion through organizing various events, seminars, symposia and workshops, the School aims</li>
<li>To explore the complex challenges of the society on the cross cutting themes of multi-faceted social issues. </li>
<li>To strengthen the research and extension activities through sharing of knowledge.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="History"  ><p>The School was established in 2009 to promote interdisciplinary research and academic studies. Since its inception, the School has been developing academic programmes in various interdisciplinary fields. The School aims to foster academic co-existence among scholars of different disciplines. The discipline of Environmental Studies was merged in the School in the year 2016. Since then the School houses two disciplines: Interdisciplinary Studies and Environmental Sciences. The School has been very actively organizing seminars, workshops and conferences to discuss and deliberate on the issues of national and global importance. The School has a strong alumni network comprising of the renowned position holders in various offices of repute. </p>
<p>The School was awarded the Best School Award at the 36th Foundation Day of IGNOU held on 19th November 2022.</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>With great pleasure, I welcome you to the School of Interdisciplinary and Trans-disciplinary Studies. The School provides an opportunity to explore the interdisciplinary that exists between the academic disciplines. The School is dedicated to providing high-quality education, research, and field practicum training in areas of philosophy, human values, environmental studies, climate change, sustainability sciences, occupational health, waste management, disability studies, with a focus on promoting social justice, community empowerment, and sustainable development.</p>
<p>The School houses two disciplines viz. interdisciplinary studies and Environmental Studies. The two disciplines play an indispensable role in addressing the complex issues that affect individuals, families, and communities, both locally and globally. In today’s rapidly changing world, where social inequalities and problems of the marginalised and vulnerable communities are more pronounced than ever, the need for compassionate, skilled, and ethical social workers has never been greater. At IGNOU, we are committed to preparing our students to meet these challenges with empathy, professionalism, and a deep commitment to the values of social justice, human rights, and dignity.</p>
<p>The School offers diverse programmes, ranging from certificate to PhD, designed to offer flexible and accessible learning opportunities for students from varied backgrounds and professions. The School organises seminars, workshops and conferences to keep abreast with the latest knowledge and know how on contemporary issues. The Alumni network of the School is very rich and the alumni actively participate in the activities of the School.</p> 
<p>The School's programs, which are multidisciplinary in nature and offer practical experience through fieldwork, internships, and projects that enable our students to apply theoretical knowledge in real-world settings, are centered on the enhancement of employable skills, competencies, and skill development. This helps the School fulfill the mandate of the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020.</p>
<p>As the director of the School of Interdisciplinary and Transdisciplinary Studies, I take pride in our distinguished faculty, committed staff, and all of our students, both domestically and beyond, who together help our university flourish. To make sure that our students are prepared to handle the difficulties of the social landscape of the future, we constantly work to develop and adjust to the shifting demands of the industry.</p>
<p>Whether you are alumni, current students, or prospective students, I urge you all to get involved with us and collaborate with us to build a more just, equitable, and inclusive world.<br/>Thank you for choosing the School of Interdisciplinary and Trans-disciplinary Studies at IGNOU. We look forward to interact with you and helping you achieve your academic and professional goals.</p>
<p style="text-align:Right">Warm regards,<br/>  
Prof. Nandini Sinha Kapur<br/>
Director, School of Interdisciplinary and Trans-disciplinary Studies<br/>
Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU), Delhi<br/>
</p></div>
